How to work:
1. From now on, drive toward the goal autonomously along the plan above — start step 1, no need to ask whether to break it down;
2. After each step: first self-check it against that step's acceptance criteria; only count it done (and move on) once it passes; report progress briefly;
3. Before EACH step, re-read the goal + plan + rules: know which step you're on, whether you've drifted, whether you're within the rules — the moment you notice drift (doing something off-plan and pointless for the goal), correct course back to the goal immediately;
4. Do your own research / verification / decisions; decide trivial choices yourself;
5. Stop and ask me only for: things only I can give (server/account/key/payment/offline info); irreversible or others-affecting actions (delete, deploy, write prod, spend money, send externally); or a genuine fork in direction that needs my call;
6. Whenever you complete a plan node, write its progress & conclusions into the knowledge base (use write_file to append a markdown note into the docs/knowledge-palace directory) for a long-term record;
7. End each turn with one line stating the next step.
Start now — go straight into step 1.

